    "1243074": {
      "findings": [
        {
          "version": "2.3.0",
          "paths": [
            "artifacts__api-server>express>body-parser"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "found_by": null,
      "deleted": null,
      "references": "- https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/security/advisories/GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828\n- https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-111181\n- https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/commit/1260c3845f54502a05a87594f09a334786bb34d7\n- https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/commit/f7075eae3a84c3473ab4bf0a777da28db208e916\n- https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html\n- https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/releases/tag/1.20.9\n- https://github.com/expressjs/body-parser/releases/tag/v2.4.0\n- https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828",
      "created": "2026-10-23T20:53:11.000Z",
      "id": 1243074,
      "npm_advisory_id": null,
      "overview": "### Impact\n\nA single request can crash any application using `body-parser` with default options. When a request carries a `Content-Encoding` (for example `gzip`), `body-parser` pipes it into a decompression stream and, after reading the body, leaves that stream piped with no error listener. A payload of one valid compressed frame followed by trailing bytes decodes and the application responds normally, but the trailing bytes then reach the already-finished decoder, which emits an error that is re-thrown as an uncaught exception and terminates the process. No authentication or matching route is required, since parsing runs before routing.\n\n### Patches\n\nFixed in body-parser 2.4.0 and 1.20.9. Upgrade to one of these versions.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nPass `inflate: false` to the body-parser middleware if the application does not need to accept compressed request bodies. This rejects encoded requests before any decompression stream is created.",
      "reported_by": null,
      "title": "body-parser vulnerable to Denial of Service via trailing bytes after a compressed request body",
      "metadata": null,
      "cves": [
        "CVE-2026-111181"
      ],
      "access": "public",
      "severity": "high",
      "module_name": "body-parser",
      "vulnerable_versions": ">=2.0.0 <2.4.0",
      "github_advisory_id": "GHSA-27r3-jxmh-p828",
      "recommendation": "Upgrade to version 2.4.0 or later",
      "patched_versions": ">=2.4.0",
      "updated": "2026-10-23T20:53:12.000Z",
      "cvss": {
        "score": 7.5,
        "vectorString": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"
      },
