    "1243079": {
      "findings": [
        {
          "version": "6.25.0",
          "paths": [
            "artifacts__gxeon-dashboard-mobile>@expo/cli>undici"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "found_by": null,
      "deleted": null,
      "references": "- https://github.com/nodejs/undici/security/advisories/GHSA-4qv8-2p9j-2685\n- https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-109924\n- https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/299162740d5f39120092277e70efacb4d151c1c6\n- https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/789ef26461c648480433846607154f52d74ec9ab\n- https://github.com/nodejs/undici/commit/c43b23fdc6b37e1283d4347408bb16800f867d9e\n- https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html\n- https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v6.29.1\n- https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v7.30.1\n- https://github.com/nodejs/undici/releases/tag/v8.12.2\n- https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-4qv8-2p9j-2685",
      "created": "2026-10-23T22:13:29.000Z",
      "id": 1243079,
      "npm_advisory_id": null,
      "overview": "### Impact\n\nundici's `EventSource` client can be driven to exhaust process memory by a malicious or compromised Server-Sent Events peer. By sending millions of tiny completed `data:` fields with no blank event separator, or a single unfinished line split across many chunks, the parser retains a growing amount of per-field and per-chunk state. The byte-based `maxEventSize` and `maxResponseSize` limits do not bound that retained state, and `maxResponseSize` is enforced on the compressed body before decompression, so a small compressed response can expand into enough retained memory to terminate the process. The application only needs to maintain an `EventSource` connection to an untrusted peer, which controls only the response. Availability is the only impact.\n\n### Patches\n\nUpgrade to `6.29.1`, `7.30.1`, or `8.12.2`, which bound the retained EventSource parser state (the number of `data` fields and buffered chunks, the unfinished-line length, and per-field byte totals) independently of the byte limits.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nNone.",
      "reported_by": null,
      "title": "undici vulnerable to Denial of Service via unbounded memory in the EventSource parser",
      "metadata": null,
      "cves": [
        "CVE-2026-109924"
      ],
      "access": "public",
      "severity": "moderate",
      "module_name": "undici",
      "vulnerable_versions": ">=6.5.0 <6.29.1",
      "github_advisory_id": "GHSA-4qv8-2p9j-2685",
      "recommendation": "Upgrade to version 6.29.1 or later",
      "patched_versions": ">=6.29.1",
      "updated": "2026-10-23T22:13:31.000Z",
      "cvss": {
        "score": 5.9,
        "vectorString": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:N/A:H"
      },
      "cwe": [
        "CWE-770"
