    "1243098": {
      "findings": [
        {
          "version": "3.1.8",
          "paths": [
            "lib__api-spec>orval>@scalar/openapi-parser>ajv>fast-uri"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "found_by": null,
      "deleted": null,
      "references": "- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-w74x-v6f9-j3xg\n- https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-110306\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/39933a1f1422986f14e2d844f552238feb40f5d4\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/597f254c86d151568511eeb9a1df761fd12520b3\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/e60e716f41d1d73717e2d803d20b68d2c6d20a0f\n- https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v2.4.8\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v3.1.9\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v4.2.3\n- https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-w74x-v6f9-j3xg",
      "created": "2026-10-23T21:41:36.000Z",
      "id": 1243098,
      "npm_advisory_id": null,
      "overview": "### Impact\n\n`fast-uri` percent-decodes the scheme component with the legacy global `unescape()` before validating it, so an input whose decoded scheme is a valid but dangerous token is emitted as a live scheme. RFC 3986 section 3.1 does not allow percent-encoding in a scheme, so no RFC or WHATWG parser treats such input as having that scheme, but `fast-uri` does.\n\nFor example, `normalize('%6Aavascript:alert(1)')` returns `javascript:alert(1)`, `resolve('https://a.example/', '%6Aavascript:alert(1)')` returns `javascript:alert(1)`, and `parse('%6Aavascript:alert(1)').scheme` returns `javascript`. The `%uXXXX` form (`%u006Aavascript:`) produces the same result, and `equal('%68ttp://a/', 'http://a/')` returns `true`.\n\nAn application that screens dangerous schemes on the raw input and then stores or renders `normalize(input)` or `resolve(base, input)` turns an inert string into an executable `javascript:`, `data:`, or `vbscript:` URL, a stored or reflected cross-site scripting vector in the consuming application. `equal()` also treats an encoded and a plain scheme as the same, which can bypass equality-based allowlists.\n\n### Patches\n\nUpgrade to `fast-uri` `2.4.8`, `3.1.9`, or `4.2.3`.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nReject input whose scheme part (before the first `:`, and before any `/`, `?`, or `#`) contains `%`. Alternatively, check `parse(x).scheme` against an allowlist after normalization and use that same parsed result rather than the raw string.",
      "reported_by": null,
      "title": "fast-uri vulnerable to URI scheme spoofing via percent-encoded scheme decoding",
      "metadata": null,
      "cves": [
        "CVE-2026-110306"
      ],
      "access": "public",
      "severity": "moderate",
      "module_name": "fast-uri",
      "vulnerable_versions": ">=3.0.0 <3.1.9",
      "github_advisory_id": "GHSA-w74x-v6f9-j3xg",
      "recommendation": "Upgrade to version 3.1.9 or later",
      "patched_versions": ">=3.1.9",
      "updated": "2026-10-23T21:41:38.000Z",
      "cvss": {
        "score": 6.1,
        "vectorString": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:L/I:L/A:N"
      },
      "cwe": [
        "CWE-172",
        "CWE-180"
      ],
