    "1243101": {
      "findings": [
        {
          "version": "3.1.8",
          "paths": [
            "lib__api-spec>orval>@scalar/openapi-parser>ajv>fast-uri"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "found_by": null,
      "deleted": null,
      "references": "- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/security/advisories/GHSA-xhq7-xmqj-769h\n- https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-110095\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/048bbd0a252971be86d6579f0dfc87f8de5b9c47\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/52774a5c35df36b0bbe439cd4c12c3dc0e50e3b9\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/7c19f8b97ec51f1f20b4e3d9d5820cb8d5176058\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/9eb8759a9825c046f57f7f695f1944bc39b88abd\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/acc5c5d60c4209571789496e1732468911c7e12a\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/commit/b110a3571c37dfcf9d1c72ce2e2e178c78d1a424\n- https://cna.openjsf.org/security-advisories.html\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v2.4.8\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v3.1.9\n- https://github.com/fastify/fast-uri/releases/tag/v4.2.3\n- https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-xhq7-xmqj-769h",
      "created": "2026-10-23T21:39:34.000Z",
      "id": 1243101,
      "npm_advisory_id": null,
      "overview": "### Impact\n\n`fast-uri`'s `normalize()` and `serialize()` apply RFC 3986 dot-segment removal (`remove_dot_segments`) to the path of a relative-path reference. RFC 3986 section 5.2.4 defines that algorithm only for the merged target path during resolution, not for the reference itself, so applied to the reference it drops leading `..` segments and can turn a document-relative reference into a root-relative one.\n\nFor example, `normalize('a/../b')` returns `/b` and `normalize('../x')` returns `x`, so `resolve(base, normalize(ref))` points at a different resource than `resolve(base, ref)`, and `equal()` treats distinct references as the same.\n\nApplications that normalize attacker-supplied or user-supplied relative references and then resolve them, or use them as cache, deduplication, or authorization keys, can have a reference escape its intended directory and point at a different resource.\n\n### Patches\n\nUpgrade to `fast-uri` `2.4.8`, `3.1.9`, or `4.2.3`.\n\n### Workarounds\n\nDo not normalize a relative reference before resolving it. Resolve it against the absolute base first, then normalize the absolute result.",
      "reported_by": null,
      "title": "fast-uri vulnerable to improper path equivalence in relative reference normalization",
      "metadata": null,
      "cves": [
        "CVE-2026-110095"
      ],
      "access": "public",
      "severity": "low",
      "module_name": "fast-uri",
      "vulnerable_versions": ">=3.0.0 <3.1.9",
      "github_advisory_id": "GHSA-xhq7-xmqj-769h",
      "recommendation": "Upgrade to version 3.1.9 or later",
      "patched_versions": ">=3.1.9",
      "updated": "2026-10-23T21:39:38.000Z",
      "cvss": {
